n-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133087671.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Mercury's massive metallic core leads to a contraction of its rocky exterior, resulting in numerous fractures and cliffs spanning hundreds of kilometers. Recent studies have uncovered fault scarps that suggest active tectonic processes are still at play on the planet. Researchers examine these formations to gain insight into Mercury's internal mechanics, with future missions expected to deliver clearer images of these relatively young tectonic anomalies.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/mercury-is-still-shrinking-after-billions-of-years-how-its-giant-cooling-core-is-cracking-the-planets-thin-crust/articleshow/133087671.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/mercury-is-still-shrinking-after-billions-of-years-how-its-giant-cooling-core-is-cracking-the-planets-thin-crust/articleshow/133087671.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-10T12:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133087778,imgsize-194726.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists discovered that animal poop triggered the evolution of life on earth]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133087453.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-discovered-that-animal-poop-travelled-across-oceans-540-million-years-ago-and-triggered-the-evolution-of-life-on-earth/articleshow/133087453.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-discovered-that-animal-poop-travelled-across-oceans-540-million-years-ago-and-triggered-the-evolution-of-life-on-earth/articleshow/133087453.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-